## Q4 -- the standing licence

* **Attack 6 — Q4.1: RAP write arm warning `idata >= N_REGISTERS` (`dev_le.c:1017-1020`).** **[UNSETTLED (NOT CHECKABLE)]**
  * Section `8.3` (`DEVICE_ACCESS(le)`) is omitted from this packet (`8.3-8.5:1-4`). While `5:S1` confirms line `1015` masks `d->reg_select = idata & (N_REGISTERS - 1)` and `2.2:24` shows the probe writes `0x13` to RAP (`rap mask`), whether the warning at `1017-1020` is latched (`(once)`) or fires on every out-of-range write, and its exact wording, cannot be verified from this message. **UNSETTLED** — file `src/devices/dev_le.c` (lines `1010-1025`) would settle it.

* **Attack 7 — Q4.2: `le_register_write`'s `uint32_t x` parameter (`8.2:839`) vs `uint64_t idata`.** **[READ / DERIVED — HOLDS (nothing to file)]**
  * In `8.2:839`, `void le_register_write(struct le_data *d, int r, uint32_t x)` receives `x` as `uint32_t`. Every LANCE CSR is 16 bits (`uint16_t reg[N_REGISTERS]`, `5:S2`), `case 0:` only inspects 16-bit `LE_*` masks (`8.2:844-881`), and `case 1:`, `case 2:`, `default:` mask `x` with `0xfffe`, `0x00ff`, and `0x0007` (`3.1:1-12`). Narrowing `uint64_t idata` to `uint32_t x` before `uint16_t` storage cannot lose any implemented bit (`6:P8`, `5:S13`). Neither a bug nor worth a records note.

* **Attack 8 — Q4.3: The two comments at `dev_le.c:986-1001` contradicting the datasheet.** **[UNSETTLED (NOT CHECKABLE)]**
  * Because `8.3` is omitted from this packet (`8.3-8.5:1-4`), lines `986-1001` are not inlined (only alluded to in `3.4:D4`, `Q1f`, `Q3e`, and `Q4.3`). The exact contradiction in lines `986-991` cannot be verified from this packet. **UNSETTLED** — file `src/devices/dev_le.c` (lines `980-1005`) would settle it.

* **Attack 9 — Q4.4: Leaving `(d->reg[2] & 0xff)` at `dev_le.c:179` (`3.2`, `8.1`) untouched.** **[DERIVED — HOLDS]**
  * At `dev_le.c:179` (`3.2:1-2`, `8.1:2`), `init_block_addr = (d->reg[1] & 0xffff) + ((d->reg[2] & 0xff) << 16)` masks `d->reg[1]` with `0xffff` and `d->reg[2]` with `0xff`. Unlike lines `180-182` (where the `if` branch becomes dead code once `d->reg[1]` is even, violating the check-that-cannot-fail rule, `3.2:3-6`), `(d->reg[2] & 0xff)` is a pure value expression on a `uint16_t` prior to `<< 16`. Leaving line `179` alone is harmless and keeps the diff minimal (`10:R10`).

* **Attack 10 — Q4.5: The `"14/15 mnemonics"` rendering line (`2.2:44-47`).** **[UNSETTLED (NOT CHECKABLE)]**
  * In `2.2:14`, the summary output prints `encodings 15/15, 17/17, 17/17, 20/20 words against the disassembler`, while `2.2:44-47` notes that `"14/15 mnemonics"` is a secondary rendering comparison caused by `b 0x` self-loop and `ori` vs `li` disassembly differences. Printing a `14/15` ratio in test output when the authoritative word check is `15/15` does invite false-alarm readings, so suppressing the mnemonic count (or labelling it `informational`) is cleaner; however, whether the frozen 18-row probe script (`2.3:13-14`) actually prints `"14/15 mnemonics"` to stdout is **UNSETTLED** — file `regress/artifacts/lecsrmask/pass1_20261025/le_csrmask_probe.frozen.py.txt` would settle it.

